 ["K",3,"Unplanned distortion in the communication process, which means the receiver gets a different message from the one the sender sent, is called:",["Noise","Feedback","Decoding","Encoding"],"Noise, such as a busy feed full of other ads, can stop the message getting through.","2026-10-21T19:56:00+05:00"],
 ["A",2,"A bank's advert shows a father proudly watching his daughter graduate, with no facts about interest rates. The advert mainly uses:",["An emotional appeal","A rational appeal","A moral appeal","Reminder advertising"],"Emotional appeals try to stir feelings that make people want to buy.","2026-10-21T19:56:00+05:00"],
 ["A",2,"A resort's video shows a well-known Maldivian singer talking about her happy stay there. Which execution style is this?",["Testimonial evidence or endorsement","Slice of life","Scientific evidence","Mood or image"],"A trusted or famous person recommending the product is a testimonial or endorsement.","2026-10-21T19:56:00+05:00"],
 ["A",2,"A telecom company sets its advertising budget to match what its main rival spends each year. Which budget method is this?",["Competitive-parity method","Affordable method","Objective-and-task method","Percentage-of-sales method"],"Competitive parity sets the budget to match competitors' spending.","2026-10-21T19:56:00+05:00"],
 ["A",3,"A juice brand wants each young adult in Malé to see its Instagram advert at least five times in one month. This goal is about:",["Frequency","Reach","Media impact","Noise"],"Frequency is how many times the average person sees the message.","2026-10-21T19:56:00+05:00"],
 ["A",2,"A new mobile network's adverts try to convince people to switch to it because its data is faster and better value. This is mainly:",["Persuasive advertising","Informative advertising","Reminder advertising","Public relations"],"Persuasive advertising builds preference as competition grows.","2026-10-21T19:56:00+05:00"]
